 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Mating",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each wire is crimped into an SXH contact, the contacts are pushed into an XHP housing, and the housing plugs into a box-shaped shrouded header on the board. The contact grips the post with two leaves. Mated, the top-entry assembly stands (9.8) mm above the board; B4B-XH-A takes XHP-4."
  },
  {
   "topic": "HA terminal",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 4-circuit version meets JEMA's HA terminal standard for home automation equipment."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Boss",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The -AM headers carry a locating boss next to circuit 1: 1.6 ±0.05 mm along the row beyond post 1 and 2 ±0.05 mm across it, into a φ1.1 +0.2/0 hole. On B1B-XH-AM the boss sits 4.35 ±0.05 mm from the single post, into a φ1.7 +0.1/0 hole."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board holes",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Top-entry headers want φ1 ±0.05 holes for 2 circuits and φ0.9 +0.1/0 for 3 or more, on a 2.5 ±0.05 mm pitch; side-entry and radial-tape parts want φ0.9 +0.1/0, glass-filled 2-circuit parts φ1 ±0.05. Pitch tolerance does not add up along the row. The hole sizes are reference values: they depend on the board and how it is drilled, and glass-cloth boards need larger holes. Layouts are drawn from the component side."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Radial tape",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "The -TV4 headers come on radial tape for automatic insertion; their board hole is chosen to suit the insertion machine. The taped leads have a partly rounded rectangular section, (φ0.7) across, and stand 2.8 mm below the body."
  }
 ],
